.Dd November 2, 2026
.Dt FD 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm fd
.Nd find files by name
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar options
.Op Ar pattern
.Op Ar path ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
searches a tree for names that match a regular expression.
It searches the current directory when no path is given, and skips hidden
files and names excluded by ignore files, including
.Pa .gitignore
and
.Pa .fdignore .
.Fl H
includes hidden files,
.Fl I
includes ignored files, and
.Fl F
matches a literal string instead of a regular expression.
.Fl t f
selects regular files;
.Fl e Ar extension
selects a file extension.
.Ql fd --help
describes the other options.
.Pp
The x86-64 GNU root installs the author's static musl build, version 10.5.0,
under
.Pa /opt/fd
when built with
.Ql GNU_AGENTS=fd
or
.Ql GNU_AGENTS=all .
.Pa /usr/bin/fd
and
.Pa /bin/fd
link to it.
The package includes
.Pa LICENSE-MIT
and
.Pa LICENSE-APACHE ;
either license may be chosen.
Its upstream manual and shell completions stay under
.Pa /opt/fd ;
the shells do not load them automatically.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Find C source files, including hidden and ignored paths:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ fd -H -I -t f -e c
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr find 1 ,
.Xr rg 1
.Pp
.Lk https://github.com/sharkdp/fd/tree/v10.5.0 "The fd manual"
